You are given a task to integrate a component from the **kinetik** motion library into this codebase.

# Scroll Velocity Marquee (`text-velocity-marquee`)

Giant looping text lines that speed up, reverse direction and skew with your scroll velocity.

## What it should do
Build a scroll-velocity marquee with Motion: `useScroll` → `useVelocity` → `useSpring(damping 50, stiffness 400)` → factor via useTransform [0,1000]→[0,5]. In `useAnimationFrame` advance a base value by baseVelocity·dt, flip direction with the velocity sign and multiply by the factor; x = wrap(−25%, −50%, base) over 4 repeated copies. Skew X ±12° from velocity.

## Project requirements
- React 19 + TypeScript, Tailwind CSS v4, shadcn/ui-style CSS variables (`background`, `foreground`, `muted`, `muted-foreground`, `border`, `card`, `primary`, `ring`). If the project lacks shadcn, set it up first (`npx shadcn@latest init`).
- Animation engine: **motion**.
- Install dependencies: `npm i motion`
- Put the component at `components/kinetik/text-velocity-marquee.tsx`.
- `cn` lives at `lib/kinetik/utils.ts` (source below).
- Shared hooks go at `lib/kinetik/core.ts` (source below).

## Non-negotiables
- **Accessibility:** aria-label holds the text once; repeated copies are aria-hidden. Reduced motion: static line.
- **Performance:** useAnimationFrame + springs; transforms only.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` (replace movement with opacity or an instant change).
- Animate only transform / opacity / filter / clip-path. No hard-coded theme colors — use CSS variables so it works in light and dark.

